<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baghdad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baghdad is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, founded in 762 by the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mansur as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>. It became one of the largest cities in the world and a great centre of trade and learning. It came under Seljuk control in 1055 and was sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1258, after which it formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and was later contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad.jpg" alt="Baghdad" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USACE HQ , JIM GORDAN, CIV, USACE · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5628442718_b10fc2c47f_o.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
